

# The request in controlled English

The same requirement, said again in the controlled English the repository's reasoner reads, one sentence a line:

Multiversion_Tree is a program.
Multiversion_Tree reads the commands from the standard_input.
Multiversion_Tree reads the commands until the end_of_input.
Every command is a line.
Every line that is blank is ignored.
Every transaction_name is a word.
Every key is an integer.
Every key that is negative is an integer.
Every b_command begins a transaction at the latest_committed_version.
Every b_command that names an active_transaction causes an error.
Every i_command stages an insertion.
Every insertion has a key.
Every i_command that names an inactive_transaction causes an error.
Every d_command stages a deletion.
Every deletion has a key.
Every d_command that names an inactive_transaction causes an error.
Every c_command commits the transaction atomically.
Every c_command applies the staged_changes.
Every staged_changes forms a new_committed_version.
Every c_command increments the commit_id.
Every c_command ends the transaction.
Every c_command that names an empty_transaction increments the commit_id.
Every c_command that names an inactive_transaction causes an error.
Every a_command aborts the transaction.
Every a_command discards the staged_changes.
Every a_command ends the transaction.
Every a_command that names an inactive_transaction causes an error.
Every r_command that names a visible_key prints "yes".
Every r_command that names an invisible_key prints "no".
Every r_command that names an inactive_transaction causes an error.
Every p_command prints the visible_keys in the ascending_order.
Every visible_key gets a line.
Every p_command that names an empty_view prints nothing.
Every p_command that names an inactive_transaction causes an error.
Every g_command that names a latest_key prints "yes".
Every g_command that names an absent_key prints "no".
Every v_command prints the latest_commit_id.
Every view holds the committed_version at the begin_snapshot.
Every view holds the staged_insertions.
Every view holds the staged_deletions.
Every transaction keeps a staged_change.
Every transaction keeps the last staged_change.
Every staged_deletion that names an invisible_key is staged.
Every commit applies the staged_changes to the latest_committed_version.
Every last_committer wins.
Every insertion that names a present_key changes nothing.
Every deletion that names an absent_key changes nothing.
Multiversion_Tree uses a B_tree for the committed_versions.
Every B_tree has a minimum_degree.
The minimum_degree is 2.
Multiversion_Tree uses a recursion for the insertion.
Multiversion_Tree uses a recursion for the deletion.
Multiversion_Tree allocates the nodes dynamically.
Multiversion_Tree has an unbounded number_of_keys.
Multiversion_Tree has an unbounded number_of_transactions.
Multiversion_Tree does not print a prompt.
Multiversion_Tree does not print a debug_output.